01  YOUR HEADLINE: THE SEO THAT GETS YOU FOUND


Most people treat their headline like a job title. It is not. It is a search keyword field.
Recruiters use LinkedIn Sales Navigator to find candidates. They type in a skill or role and the algorithm surfaces profiles that match. Your headline is one of the first places it looks.

How Sales Navigator actually works
Recruiter opens Sales Navigator and types in a role or skill
LinkedIn scans headlines, skills, and experience sections for keyword matches
Profiles with the right keywords appear at the top. Everyone else is invisible.

What a weak headline looks like
Weak
Software Engineer at AmazonThis tells the algorithm nothing beyond your current employer.


What a strong headline looks like
Strong
Software Engineer @ Amazon | Backend Systems | AWS | Java | Distributed Systems | UIUC CS 2025This hits multiple search terms at once. Every keyword is a new reason to show up in a search.


Headline formula
Current role and company
2 to 3 core technical skills
1 domain you specialize in
Education or credential if relevant

Quick Action
Rewrite your headline right now. Open LinkedIn, go to edit profile, and add at least 4 keywords. It takes 3 minutes.


