02  YOUR ABOUT SECTION: THE SALES PITCH


Once a recruiter finds your profile from a keyword search, your About section is what makes them stop scrolling. It needs to answer three questions immediately: Who are you, what have you done, and why should I reach out to you right now.

What to include
A human opening line that is not just your job title
The most impressive thing you have shipped, built, or fixed with a real number attached
Your specific skills and the scale at which you have used them
What you are open to and how to reach you

What to avoid
Passionate engineer seeking new opportunities says nothing
Long walls of text with no white space
Generic buzzwords like results-oriented or self-starter
Copying from your resume verbatim

