03  EXPERIENCE: WRITE PROOF, NOT DESCRIPTIONS


Most LinkedIn experience sections read like job descriptions copied from an HR doc. They list responsibilities. Nobody cares about responsibilities. Recruiters care about results.

The difference
Weak
Led a team and improved system performance.
Strong
Led 6 engineers to cut API latency by 40%, shipping 2 weeks ahead of schedule.


The three things every bullet needs
Action: what you did
Metric: what the result was
Keywords: what you used to do it

Template
[Action verb] [what you built or fixed] using [technology], resulting in [specific metric or outcome].


Keyword strategy
List every technology, language, and framework you touched in that role
Include team size, system scale, and user impact wherever you can
Recruiters search for Java, Python, AWS, Kubernetes separately. Each one you add is a new reason to show up.

Quick Action
Go to your most recent role and rewrite 2 bullets using the formula above. Add the name of every technology you used, even if it was minor.


