06  ACTIVITY: THE ALGORITHM REWARDS WHO SHOWS UP


Active LinkedIn users get 10x more profile views than dormant ones. You do not need to go viral. You just need to show up consistently.

Three ways to stay active without burning out
Post original content once a week. Share what you are building, learning, or figuring out. One post a week is enough to keep the algorithm surfacing you.
Comment on posts in your field. A specific thoughtful comment on a well-followed person's post puts your name in front of their entire audience. Do this 3 times a week.
Repost with your own take. Find a post you genuinely agree with, repost it, and add 2 to 3 sentences about why it matters. Counts as activity. Takes 90 seconds.

Content ideas if you have no idea what to post
A problem you solved at work and how you solved it
A tool you discovered that saved you time
Something you got wrong and what you learned
A career decision you made and why
A resource that helped you and why it helped

Quick Action
Write one LinkedIn post today. 3 to 5 sentences about something you learned this week. Post it and leave it.


